meta {
  name: Get Public Share
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/rag/shares/{{shareCode}}?invite={{shareInviteToken}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  PUBLIC read of a share link — no authentication required (the backend
  ignores the Authorization header when present). Private shares REQUIRE the
  access token from the invite email as `?invite=<token>`, otherwise 403
  PRIVATE_SHARE.

  Response: { code, title, authorName, isPrivate, expiresAt, createdAt,
              conversationId, turns: [...] }

  Each snapshot turn may carry `attachments: [{ "documentId": "...", "title": "laporan.pdf" }]`
  baked at share time — id + title only. Titles are visible on the public page
  (static cards); the documents themselves are NOT openable (preview endpoint
  requires auth + tenant ownership).

  - 403 PRIVATE_SHARE when the link is invite-only and the token is missing
    or wrong.
  - 404 when the link does not exist or has expired (expired rows are
    lazy-deleted on read).
  - Public viewers only receive the snapshot columns — tenant_id / created_by /
    access_token are never exposed (column-level grants + RLS).
}
